# All binary content is stored in Cloudflare R2 via QPR-LFS-R2 pointers.
# The git-lfs filter is intentionally DISABLED — git-lfs is not used for storage.
#
# The `filter=lfs` lines are stripped to prevent git-lfs from intercepting
# our custom QPR-LFS-R2 pointer files. Files committed as QPR pointers
# are served from R2 via the qpr-file-server worker.
#
# New files added via the contribution portal are uploaded to R2 and
# committed as QPR-LFS-R2 pointers — git-lfs is never involved.
#
# The `:(attr:filter=lfs)` git grep attribute still works for identifying
# binary files by extension in scripts/r2-sync-cleanup.js.
#
# All globs below intentionally have filter=lfs stripped.
# DO NOT re-add `filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs` to these lines.

*.pdf -text
*.doc -text
*.docx -text
*.ppt -text
*.pptx -text
*.xls -text
*.xlsx -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.png -text
*.gif -text
*.webp -text
*.bmp -text
*.svg -text
*.zip -text
